{"id": "xbelgium", "name": "Hautes Fagnes (High Fens)", "short": "High Fens", "place": "Belgium", "lat": 50.5, "lon": 6.1, "side": "r", "cont": "Europe", "country": "Belgium", "blurb": "Rain-fed raised bogs where peat moss, heather and the last black grouse hold on.", "tip": {"id": "rain", "title": "Take away the rain", "text": "The bogs live on rainfall alone. Set Rainfall to -100% and watch the peat moss and heather fade, then the voles, grouse and predators that depend on them."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Hautes Fagnes (High Fens)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hautes_Fagnes"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: High Fens - Eifel Nature Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Fens_%E2%80%93_Eifel_Nature_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Black grouse", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_grouse"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Sphagnum", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sphagnum"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Hautes Fagnes", "icon": "water", "tier": "overview", "kind": "Lakes & wetlands", "park": true, "nodes": [{"id": "sphagnum", "sp": "sphagnum", "xh": 0.1, "ic": "algae"}, {"id": "heather", "sp": "calluna vulgaris", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "Small evergreen shrub of the heath and moorland. Sheep graze it in the High Fens, and deer browse it elsewhere."}, {"id": "bilberry", "sp": "vaccinium myrtillus", "xh": 0.5, "desc": "Low berry shrub of the moorland. Its leaves and berries feed black grouse, deer and voles."}, {"id": "molinia", "sp": "molinia caerulea", "xh": 0.7}, {"id": "spruce", "sp": "picea abies", "xh": 0.9, "desc": "Planted widely around the fens. The plantations are listed among the causes of damage to the bogs, but the trees feed deer and grouse."}, {"id": "roe", "sp": "capreolus capreolus", "xh": 0.08, "name": "Roe deer", "wiki": "Roe deer", "desc": "Small deer of woodland edges and moor. It browses heather, bilberry and young spruce, and is listed among the mammals of the High Fens."}, {"id": "red", "sp": "cervus elaphus", "xh": 0.24, "name": "Red deer", "wiki": "Red deer", "desc": "Large deer of forest and moor that browses heather and bilberry shoots.", "ic": "elk"}, {"id": "vole", "sp": "myodes glareolus", "xh": 0.4, "desc": "Small rodent of heath and scrub that eats bilberry and other low plants. It is a main food of many predators."}, {"id": "hare", "sp": "lepus europaeus", "xh": 0.56, "desc": "Grazer of grass and herbs on open ground, and prey for foxes, wildcats and birds of prey."}, {"id": "grouse", "sp": "lyrurus tetrix", "xh": 0.72}, {"id": "hopper", "sp": "omocestus viridulus", "xh": 0.9, "wiki": "Common green grasshopper", "desc": "Grassland grasshopper recorded across the plateau, feeding on grasses and eaten by frogs and birds."}, {"id": "frog", "sp": "rana temporaria", "xh": 0.1}, {"id": "stoat", "sp": "mustela erminea", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "Slender weasel that hunts voles, shrews, young hares and small birds."}, {"id": "adder", "sp": "vipera berus", "xh": 0.5, "desc": "Venomous snake of heath and bog edges, feeding on voles, lizards and frogs."}, {"id": "buzzard", "sp": "buteo buteo", "xh": 0.7, "desc": "Common bird of prey over the plateau, taking voles, hares, frogs and snakes."}, {"id": "kite", "sp": "milvus milvus", "xh": 0.9}, {"id": "fox", "sp": "vulpes vulpes", "xh": 0.3, "tl": 4, "desc": "Generalist hunter that eats voles, hares, frogs and ground birds. Wikipedia names it among the predators of black grouse."}, {"id": "wildcat", "sp": "felis silvestris", "xh": 0.7, "tl": 4, "desc": "Shy forest cat that hunts voles, hares, birds and frogs."}, {"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Summer light drives the growth of the heath and moor plants."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "rainfall", "xh": 0.35, "desc": "The raised bogs are fed by 